{"pages":[{"w":612.0,"h":792.0,"s":[[13.889,2.206,18.17,3.8,3.431,"EQUINOX"],[13.889,5.306,14.953,1.205,1.078,"Q U A N T I T A T I V E"],[69.444,2.807,15.359,1.643,1.471,"India Equity Research"],[69.444,4.27,11.266,1.46,1.307,"22 November 2026"],[13.889,10.995,31.168,3.651,3.268,"Dixon Technologies"],[13.889,14.731,33.985,2.373,2.124,"Memory prices lift revenue, not profit"],[13.889,20.845,52.934,1.809,1.634,"Dixon has risen 19% since its Q2 FY27 results on 30 October (NIFTY +12%)"],[13.889,22.289,52.931,1.809,1.634,"and at ₹13,120 trades at 94x FY26 adjusted EPS of ₹139.6 and 78x FY27"],[13.889,23.733,52.951,1.809,1.634,"consensus. The headline looked poor: profit after minorities fell 49% to ₹344 cr,"],[13.889,25.177,52.934,1.809,1.634,"almost all of it a smaller fair-value gain on the Aditya Infotech stake (₹57 cr"],[13.889,26.621,52.931,1.809,1.634,"against ₹465 cr). Excluding it, profit rose 19% to ₹293 cr on revenue up 47% to"],[13.889,28.065,52.934,1.809,1.634,"₹21,794 cr. Operating profit rose only 6%: the margin fell to 2.7% from 3.8% as"],[13.889,29.509,52.936,1.809,1.634,"the first mobile PLI scheme expired and dearer memory chips, passed through at"],[13.889,30.954,41.095,1.809,1.634,"cost, swelled revenue. H1 free cash flow was ₹980 cr negative."],[13.889,33.439,52.931,1.809,1.634,"1) Phones: management guides 33-34m units this year and 55-60m in FY28 with"],[13.889,34.883,52.936,1.809,1.634,"the Vivo joint venture; we take 50m, with Vivo at 12m in its first year against"],[13.889,36.328,52.992,1.809,1.634,"18-20m guided. 2) Mobile and EMS margin stays near 2.6-2.8% until display"],[13.889,37.772,52.934,1.809,1.634,"and camera modules scale: FY28E EPS of ₹244 is 11% below consensus (₹274)"],[13.889,39.216,52.931,1.809,1.634,"on revenue 3% above. 3) As management expects, receivables unwind by March"],[13.889,40.684,52.934,1.809,1.634,"as incentive money arrives, so FY28E free cash flow is ₹947 cr. Our EPS is"],[13.889,42.128,52.934,1.809,1.634,"adjusted profit after minorities; Dixon’s reported EPS (₹271.59 for FY26)"],[13.889,43.572,20.844,1.809,1.634,"divides profit before minorities."],[13.889,46.034,52.931,1.809,1.634,"Our Dec-27 target of ₹9,100 averages two methods. The peer-median forward"],[13.889,47.502,52.964,1.809,1.634,"P/E of 40x (Kaynes, Amber, PG Electroplast, Syrma, Avalon) on twelve-month-"],[13.889,48.946,52.934,1.809,1.634,"forward EPS of ₹289, plus the Aditya stake at ₹148, gives ₹11,688. A ten-year"],[13.889,50.39,52.931,1.809,1.634,"DCF at 12%, plus cash, less minorities, gives ₹6,430 (₹7,650 at 11%). The price"],[13.889,51.834,52.936,1.809,1.634,"needs free cash flow to grow 31% a year to FY37E, against our 17%. What"],[13.889,53.278,52.931,1.809,1.634,"would prove us wrong: management’s FY28 plan, 57.5m phones and a 90 bp"],[13.889,54.722,52.931,1.809,1.634,"margin gain, is worth ₹16,408 on the peer multiple. Risk: ₹1,110 cr of incentive"],[13.889,56.167,52.931,1.809,1.634,"income for over-performance awaits government sign-off (₹577 cr owed onward"],[13.889,57.611,9.783,1.809,1.634,"to a customer)."],[13.889,60.098,13.042,1.643,1.471,"Price Performance"],[14.451,68.709,2.306,1.022,0.915,"8,000"],[13.961,66.942,2.796,1.022,0.915,"10,000"],[13.961,65.174,2.796,1.022,0.915,"12,000"],[13.961,63.407,2.796,1.022,0.915,"14,000"],[13.961,61.639,2.796,1.022,0.915,"16,000"],[17.913,69.404,2.796,1.022,0.915,"Jan 26"],[22.539,69.404,2.796,1.022,0.915,"Apr 26"],[27.326,69.404,2.47,1.022,0.915,"Jul 26"],[32.08,69.404,2.96,1.022,0.915,"Oct 26"],[18.561,70.575,3.398,1.275,1.111,"DIXON ("],[21.962,70.601,0.618,1.241,1.111,"₹"],[22.574,70.575,0.303,1.275,1.111,")"],[25.658,70.575,7.901,1.275,1.111,"NIFTY 50 (rebased)"],[19.183,71.735,1.972,1.387,1.209,"YTD"],[24.251,71.735,1.433,1.387,1.209,"1m"],[29.624,71.735,1.433,1.387,1.209,"3m"],[34.446,71.735,1.984,1.387,1.209,"12m"],[15.277,72.8,1.691,1.387,1.209,"Abs"],[18.816,72.8,2.26,1.387,1.209,"8.5%"],[23.332,72.8,2.26,1.387,1.209,"8.4%"],[27.571,72.8,3.394,1.